    rdfs:label "Grates"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_metal_machinery_hardware/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a register-stove, or cast-iron frame with fire-bars for a sitting-room, &c. for holding fuel, and making a fire in. Grate, or grid, is also a plate with iron bars for sewers, drains, &c. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 191]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_metal_machinery_hardware; processing_state=manufactured): Named tool, ironware, arm or instrument left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 1 rows, 1840–1840. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×1. Units: Number ×1. Top routes: Montreal and Quebec → British North America ×1."@en ;
